# Regional tour reading notes

The shared regional and whole-body Guided learning player has a collapsed
**Read tour notes** disclosure. It shows the existing ordered stop titles,
captions and references without starting playback or requiring the 3D renderer
to be ready. The current source has 53 regional tours and 317 stops.

Opening, focusing or pressing within the reading disclosure synchronously pauses
playback and suspends the optional paused-stop imaging link. Closing it never
resumes playback. Escape closes the disclosure and returns focus to its summary;
IME composition, prevented events and detached disclosures are left alone.

The same existing tour/source/frame admission is required. An unresolved source
does not expose a reading outline. Renderer or model delivery failure does not
substitute anatomy, enable a quiz, unlock an imaging case or mark the tour
complete. Existing scene recovery and Exit controls remain available.

The text is the current authored draft, not independently validated anatomy or
new material inferred from a missing model. Reading does not record scores,
progress, clinical review or publication approval. References remain links, not
redistributed diagrams. Only absolute HTTP/HTTPS links without credentials are
rendered, in a clearly identified new tab.

This first reading outline covers the shared regional player. Dedicated shoulder,
nested eye/CSF and independent specimen players retain their own teaching and
review scopes; they do not acquire this reader or any approval by association.

Source and component checks do not establish assistive-technology, real WebGL,
authenticated Website or acquired-study acceptance. Test those actual journeys
separately before release. No new asset, dependency, font, dataset or service is
required.
